<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">An Error Trap</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;Entrapta fixes everything when everyone else isnâ€™t looking. Queen Angella has been rescued from the Portal, her own personal hell of demons and darkness, but she isnâ€™t out of the Whispering Woods yet. Magical fluctuations are diminishing her strength and worse yet, the princess magic is being lost. The BFS is struggling to figure out why, and what this means for them. What would a universe be without the magic they fought so hard for? What grief would that bring to the tenuous happiness that the BFS has thrived on?&lt;br /&gt;Surely there is a scientific explanation for this.&lt;br /&gt;And there's only one person who is going to find it.&lt;br /&gt;â€”â€”&lt;br /&gt;Welcome our Entrapta POV fanfic! It's the latest part of character perspective novellas of the BFS in a post-Prime universe. A challenging one for sure but weâ€™ve been getting consistent feedback that itâ€™s not just good, but the best. This is a view of Adora/Catra, Bow/Glimmer from a perspective that is very unique and how it impacts Entrapta as a person. She's struggled for friendship and has only known being a friend as being useful for fixing things, but her interactions with other people are being strained. What's a scientist to do? Buckle up for a journey thatâ€™s unlike any other.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>4theHonourofGrÃ¤yskÃ¼ll (AVAwolfpack), But_Its_For_Science (DakianDelomast), DakianDelomast</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
      <dc:subject>
